+# Full study — Furstenberg times-p, times-q convergence
+
+The frozen proposition concerns the equivalence between the answer `False`
+and a universal convergence assertion for atomless invariant probability
+measures on the additive circle.  The exact source theorem is
+`Arxiv.id2303_01089.conjecture_1_4`, from the pinned
+`FormalConjectures.Arxiv.2303.01089.FurstenbergTimesPTimesQ` module.
+
+The dossier preserves every quantified hypothesis, map, filter, limit and
+measure expression through the source binding.  The human reconstruction is
+organized by source binding, transport, machine closure and release review;
+no hypotheses or exceptional cases are dropped.  The source provider is
+explicitly not treated as proof authority because its frozen record contains
+`sorryAx`.
